GDN chunk-state kernel at 16 warps instead of 4.

The native SM75 state kernel (gdn-chunk-state.patch) runs 128 threads with a
48 KiB static shared tile, so one CTA per SM: 4 warps, ~6% occupancy, and the
per-chunk serial chain of ~5 barriers and six shared round trips dominates.
Nothing about the tile changes here; the same four tiles per warp become one
per warp across 16 warps, and the eight projection tiles are computed by the
first eight warps while the rest proceed to the barrier.

Bitwise identical outputs (h, v_new, final state) against the 4-warp kernel;
measured 5.67 -> 1.98 ms per 2048-token chunk per layer (3.1x) with one CTA
per SM and no spills (103 registers at 8 warps, under the 128-register cap
for 512 threads).

